\section{Remotes}{

\code{remote} can be a folder on a shared disk (e.g. \code{"/mnt/fast/ledgers"}), a Google Drive
folder (a \code{drive.google.com} URL or a folder id; the folder is created only by
\code{CacheGeoWrite()}), or a read-only URL (the ledger is \code{remote/file}; \code{CacheGeoWrite()}
stops). With no \code{remote} the ledger is the local file only.

To share a ledger through Google Drive, create a folder, share it "Anyone with the link"
as a viewer, and give the folder's URL as \code{remote} to everyone. Only the people who write
need a Google login.
}

